# game-data/ is CONTENT ONLY: the CSV/Lua registry, the ~1750 .map terrain files, SObj.tbl. Everything
# here is authored, is identical on every deployment, and is READ-ONLY to a running server.
#
# This was its own repository until game-data merged into Project1998, and it used to also be the directory
# the server WROTE into — the SQLite database, the character store, the staff rosters and the logs all sat
# alongside these files — and most of this file was the list of runtime filenames that had to be kept out of
# the history. That list is gone because the thing it was guarding against is gone: live state now lives in
# state/, a sibling directory nothing here can see (see Shared/RepoPaths.cs).
#
# The rules kept below are local to content authoring, which is why they stay here next to the content
# rather than moving up to the root .gitignore. The first is insurance for the case where somebody points
# P1998_STATE back at a content checkout: it should never happen, and committing a database full of player
# accounts is expensive enough to be worth three lines.
project1998.db
project1998.db-*
chars/
*.log

# ---- Editor/tool backups made before a bulk CSV rewrite ----
# The rewritten file is the content; the pre-image is scratch. Includes the one-off *.pre-<thing>-restore
# snapshots taken before a destructive bulk edit.
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
*.pre-*
